2025-07-17 21:21:50 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:181 - 创建分块 0: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-17 21:21:50 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:182 - 创建分块 0: 数据 = {'id': 'a2f51488-c724-4472-8bbb-6d082983ca59', 'document_id': 'c04f58cb-a224-4dbd-952d-01fb3c7d6edf', 'content': '# Novel natural rubber composites with geopolymer filler\nHassarutai Yangthong | Skulrat Pichaiyut | Saysunee Jumrat | Suwaluk Wisunthorn Charoen Nakason\nFaculty of Science and Industrial Technology, Prince of Songkla University, Surat Thani, Thailand\n## Correspondence\nSuwaluk Wisunthorn and Charoen Nakason, Faculty of Science and Industrial Technology, Prince of Songkla University, Surat Thani, Thailand.\nEmails: suwaluk.w@psu.ac.th (SW); charoen.na@psu.ac.th (CN)\nFunding information\nPSU NR-IRI (Natural Rubber Innovation Research Institute, Grant/Award Number: SIT590315S\n## Abstract\nThe main objective of this study was to apply geopolymer (GP) particles as novelty fillers in natural rubber (NR) composites with various loadings $(0,{10},{20},{30}$ , and 40 phr). Influence of GP particles on cure characteristics, mechanical, dynamic, thermal, and morphological properties of the NR/geopolymer composites was investigated. It was found that incorporation of geopolymer particles significantly affected the cure characteristics and the mechanical properties. That is, faster curing was observed due to acceleration by metal oxide impurities. It was also found that ${100}\\%$ modulus and tensile strength increased with the addition of ${10}\\mathrm{{phr}}\\mathrm{{GP}}$ . This is attributed to the physical interactions of GP particles with NR molecules. In addition, the Payne effect and improved thermal stability were also observed in the GP-filled NR composites. It was concluded that ${10}\\mathrm{{phr}}$ of GP in NR composites might be suitable for some industrial applications.\n## KEYWORDS\ncomposites, geopolymer, mechanical properties, natural rubber, thermal properties\n## 1 INTRODUCTION', 'chunk_index': 0, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': {'paragraph_index': 0, 'original_length': 56}}}
2025-07-17 21:21:50 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:195 - 分块 0 创建成功: a2f51488-c724-4472-8bbb-6d082983ca59
2025-07-17 21:21:50 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:181 - 创建分块 1: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-17 21:21:50 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:182 - 创建分块 1: 数据 = {'id': '86005d6e-6e7c-4b9a-99c6-0733d6a8af34', 'document_id': 'c04f58cb-a224-4dbd-952d-01fb3c7d6edf', 'content': 'with NR molecules. In addition, the Payne effect and improved thermal stability were also observed in the GP-filled NR composites. It was concluded that ${10}\\mathrm{{phr}}$ of GP in NR composites might be suitable for some industrial applications. ## KEYWORDS composites, geopolymer, mechanical properties, natural rubber, thermal properties ## 1 INTRODUCTION Polymer composites combine a polymer matrix with fillers. They are attractive in industrial applications and for academic research, due to control of the material properties. Natural rubber (NR) as a green and renewable polymer is widely used as a raw polymer material industrially, including in automotive parts and tires, because of its excellent mechanical and elastic properties. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack 1\\right\\rbrack }$ However, fillers are necessary in most cases to modify the NR properties for specific applications. A wide variety of particulate fillers are used in the rubber industry for multiple purposes, including reinforcement, reduced material costs, and improved processing. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack 2\\right\\rbrack }$ The most important fillers in rubber compounding are the conventional synthetic fillers based on carbon black and silica. They reinforce and enhance various properties such as tear strength, tensile strength, hardness, and abrasion resistance. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack 3\\right\\rbrack }$ The incorporation of solid particles with large specific surface, such as synthetic silica, quartz, carbonaceous materials, and metal oxides, provided ample filler surface to interact with the rubber molecules, and hence these are very effective in improving rubber properties. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack 4\\right\\rbrack }$ Synthetic silicas, for instance precipitated silica, possess siloxane and acidic silanol groups (Si-OH), ${}^{\\left\\lbrack 5\\right\\rbrack }$ and have also been widely used in the polymer industries. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack 6\\right\\rbrack }$ Typically the silica surfaces are hydrophilic, so they have strong tendency to adsorb moisture. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack 7\\right\\rbrack }$ Furthermore, when large amounts of silica are added, the compound viscosity is increased substantially due to strong silica-silica interactions, ${}^{\\left\\lbrack 8\\right\\rbrack }$ and the production of these conventional fillers is highly energy-consuming. Thus, alternative fillers from renewable resources are of considerable interest to improve the properties of rubber while improving sustainability and green aspects of the rubber life cycle.', 'chunk_index': 1, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
