2025-07-17 21:21:50 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:182 - 创建分块 10: 数据 = {'id': 'f6e47988-864a-43a1-b917-43018319c8da', 'document_id': 'c04f58cb-a224-4dbd-952d-01fb3c7d6edf', 'content': '5</td></tr><tr><td>Zirconium oxide $\\left( {\\mathrm{{ZrO}}}_{2}\\right)$</td><td>-</td><td>0.1</td></tr></table> Figure 2 shows the particle size distributions of geopolymer and fly ash. It can be seen that the FA had a narrower size distribution than the GP but with larger ${13.5\\mu }\\mathrm{m}$ mean particle size than the ${9.5\\mu }\\mathrm{m}$ of GP (Table 3). It is also seen that both FA and GP had similar pH and density (Table 3). Table 4 shows the chemical compositions of FA and GP. It is seen that these two fillers had otherwise similar chemical compositions, but the geopolymer had more silicon dioxide $\\left( {\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}\\right)$ . Also, some compounds were only found in GP, including phosphorus pentoxide, manganese oxide, barium oxide, sodium oxide, and zirconium oxide.\nParticle morphologies of the geopolymer and the fly ash were assessed from SEM images, shown in Figure 3. It is clear that the FA had somewhat larger particle size than the GP. Furthermore, the spherical geopolymer particles had smooth surfaces but irregular shapes. On the other hand, the fly ash particles were solid spheres with some hollow ceno-spheres. Furthermore, the FA and GP had similar ranges of particle size from $< {1\\mu }\\mathrm{m}$ to larger than ${50\\mu }\\mathrm{m}$ , with the typical particle size $< {20\\mu }\\mathrm{m}$ . Also, it is noted that only about ${10}\\%$ of the particles are larger than ${30\\mu }\\mathrm{m}$ .\nTABLE 4 Chemical compositions of fly ash and geopolymer particles\n![01974484-c8d5-72ac-a6d1-acf6a850ed04_4_903_134_731_635_0.jpg](images/01974484-c8d5-72ac-a6d1-acf6a850ed04_4_903_134_731_635_0.jpg)\nFIGURE 4 Fourier-transform infrared spectroscopy spectra of geopolymer and fly ash particles [Colour figure can be viewed at wileyonlinelibrary.com]\n### 3.2 | Geopolymerization and chemical composition of geopolymer and fly ash particles', 'chunk_index': 10, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
