6 Cure characteristic of gum and FA- and GP-filled NR vulcanizates with various geopolymer loadings and 10 phr of fly ash\n![01974484-c8d5-72ac-a6d1-acf6a850ed04_7_128_1449_1010_753_0.jpg](images/01974484-c8d5-72ac-a6d1-acf6a850ed04_7_128_1449_1010_753_0.jpg)\nFIGURE 8 Schematic representations of geopolymer (GP) and fly ash (FA) structures and their dispersion in the natural rubber (NR) matrix, for the NR/GP (a) and NR/FA (b) composites\n![01974484-c8d5-72ac-a6d1-acf6a850ed04_8_626_133_1014_781_0.jpg](images/01974484-c8d5-72ac-a6d1-acf6a850ed04_8_626_133_1014_781_0.jpg)\nFIGURE 9 Stress-strain curves of gum, fly ash- and geopolymer (GP)-filled natural rubber vulcanizates with various geopolymer loadings or 10 phr fly ash. (The insert provides magnified view of below 100% extensions.)\n### 3.5 | Mechanical properties', 'chunk_index': 16, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
